From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luke Craig <lacraig3@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 20:40:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] system: build the penguin syscall engine and host-side OSI

system/penguin-syscalls.c: igloo's syscall hook model served in QEMU
(penguin_syscall_* C ABI for penguin's cffi): filters (args, comm, pid,
fd path, exe), skip/modify, the callback protocol (READ, READ_STR, WRITE,
SYSCALL, ABORT) with runs held across pagein faults and injected calls,
the guard, the reaper and the exec hook.  system/penguin-osi.c: process,
fd, mm and namespace walks from the kernel's ISF layout.

Vendored sources: src/system/penguin-syscalls.c, penguin-osi.c,
src/include/system/penguin-syscalls.h, penguin-osi.h.
---
 system/meson.build | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/system/meson.build b/system/meson.build
index 4f8de182a383d804d8771b279af6d49ce72bd07e..4e3cbb680979b9fd27cf29577f4a02a69016a844 100644
--- a/system/meson.build
+++ b/system/meson.build
@@ -18,6 +18,8 @@ system_ss.add(files(
   'memory_mapping.c',
   'memory.c',
   'penguin.c',
+  'penguin-syscalls.c',
+  'penguin-osi.c',
   'physmem.c',
   'qdev-monitor.c',
   'qtest.c',
